    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.files\n\n### Description\n\nI sometimes accidentally enter insert mode while navigating in the mini.files window. This causes the border color of the window to change (signalling a change to the file system) even though nothing changed (see below). The color stays like this even if I leave insert mode again.\r\n\r\n \r\n![image](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/assets/40792180/0b38bbc6-7fb2-46fc-8562-50afa7ff2b7a)\r\n\r\n\r\nWould it be possible to only change the behavior so that the window border is only updated if the buffer contents changed? Currently, it seems to be triggered on InsertEnter.",
